# Phase 2 (Platform IO): `stdin` is the always-open standard-input handle
# (§15.4). `stdin.slurp()` reads ALL of stdin VERBATIM (terminators intact, no
# chomp). The gate pipes io_stdin.stdin to BOTH engines. A second slurp sees the
# stream already consumed and yields "" — `stdin` references share one stream,
# matching the interpreter, which reads from a single input source.
sub main(): Int {
    print("first:[" ~ stdin.slurp() ~ "]")
    print("second:[" ~ stdin.slurp() ~ "]")
    0
}
